The SQL queries in this directory are TPC-H benchmark queries augmented with a
vector-search range predicate over embedding columns ("TPC-H+V"). This directory
also contains query_params.jsonl — committed (q, D) query parameters whose vectors
are de-minimis samples of the open datasets attributed below.

--- TPC-H ---

TPC-H is a decision support benchmark developed and maintained by the Transaction
Processing Performance Council (TPC). The benchmark specification and queries are
Copyright (C) 1993-2022 Transaction Processing Performance Council. All rights reserved.

These queries are used here solely for non-commercial benchmarking and research purposes
in accordance with the TPC Fair Use Policy (https://www.tpc.org/tpc_documents_current_versions/pdf/tpc_fair_use_policy.pdf).

The source of the benchmark specification is: https://www.tpc.org/tpch/

--- Vector augmentation (TPC-H+V) ---

The idea of augmenting TPC-H with embedding columns and vector-search predicates
is drawn from:

    Exqutor: Extended Query Optimizer for Vector-augmented Analytical Queries.
    arXiv:2512.09695. https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.09695

("TPC-H+V" above is our informal nickname for this augmented dataset, not the
paper's benchmark name.)

The SQL in this directory is authored independently from the public TPC-H
specification (https://www.tpc.org/tpch/); it is NOT copied from the Exqutor
paper's accompanying repository, which is licensed CC BY-NC 4.0. Only the
augmentation scheme (which tables carry embeddings, and the shape of the
pgvector range predicate) is taken from the paper. The embedding columns
(part.p_text_embedding, partsupp.ps_image_embedding, partsupp.ps_text_embedding,
partsupp.ps_tag) are generated deterministically by testdata/generate_testdata.sh.

--- Committed query vectors (query_params.jsonl) ---

query_params.jsonl stores ~100 (q, D) pairs. The `q` vectors are de-minimis
samples derived from two open datasets (a few dozen vectors each), redistributed
here for reproducible benchmarking:

  DEEP1B (image queries) — Licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
    The `q` of each "image" entry is a vector from the DEEP1B public query set.
    Source: https://research.yandex.com/blog/benchmarks-for-billion-scale-similarity-search
    (big-ann-benchmarks DEEP dataset, storage.yandexcloud.net/yandex-research/ann-datasets/DEEP/).
    Attribution: Yandex Research, DEEP1B / DEEP10M billion-scale ANN benchmark.

  GloVe 6B (text queries) — Public domain, released under the PDDL 1.0
    (https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/pddl/1-0/).
    The `q` of each "text" entry is the mean of GloVe 100d word-vectors over a
    short TPC-H-vocabulary phrase (the same mean used for the text columns).
    Source: GloVe, Stanford NLP (https://nlp.stanford.edu/projects/glove/).

The D (distance threshold) of every entry is computed locally with DuckDB
array_distance (k-th-nearest over the loaded vectors); see gen_query_params.py.
The full source datasets are fetched locally by testdata/fetch_embeddings.sh and
are NOT redistributed (testdata/embeddings-cache/ is gitignored).
